    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0254" n="180" xml:id="pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/772</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-08-24T19:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 24, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 28, 6 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1660. Answering confidential circular August 18, received 21st.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d237-f1"/> Minister for Foreign Affairs says French and Italian
                    Ambassadors favor no reply to the Pope’s note, British Ambassador disagrees but
                    considers haste unnecessary. Russia feels no reference to her in note is excuse
                    for no reply, but one probably will be made after conferring with Allies, and if
                    so, Minister for Foreign Affairs thinks that will be firmly negative.</p>
                <closer>[<signed> Francis</signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
